  "body": "**Blocked by:** #97\n\n## Context\n\nUsers need to compose without losing reading context and reply with correct structured recipients and sender alias.\n\n## Task\n\nAdd a floating, minimizable new-message window independent of inline thread reply. Support structured To/Cc/Bcc, reply, and reply-all from the stored envelope. Provide a plain From dropdown over registered aliases. Default it to the persisted receiving alias of the message being replied to, otherwise the current folder/account context, otherwise the primary address. Saving uses `email.draft.create`; sending uses `email.send`. Preserve unsent content when minimized, when send is rejected, and across reading-pane navigation.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- Compose lifecycle, recipients, sender selection, draft/save/send integration, and inline reply.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- New SMTP behavior, contact autocomplete beyond existing People data, and rich signature management.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Compose can be minimized and restored without data loss.\n- Reply-all is derived from structured envelope fields.\n- From defaults follow the specified fallback order and remain user-overridable.\n- A rejected send leaves an editable draft and visible error.\n",
